# Cursor marks for crlf_line_endings.cfg — the CRLF-input fixture
# (chunt-ro9). The .cfg bytes are CRLF-terminated (git keeps them
# byte-exact via .gitattributes); the document layer normalizes them to LF
# before parsing, so these coordinates — 0-indexed (LSP Position
# semantics) — are exactly what a real editor sends for the CRLF buffer:
# per-line characters address identical text, and no editor can place a
# cursor on the CR itself.
#
# Format:  <line>:<col> <feature> <optional free-form note>

# hover marks ------------------------------------------------------------
5:0 hover        interface keyword -> docstring

# definition / references marks ------------------------------------------
6:17 definition     on acl reference "ACL1" -> its definition at 2:24
9:17 definition     on undefined acl reference "ACL2" -> <none>
6:17 references     on acl reference "ACL1" -> its own site only
2:24 references-decl on the acl definition "ACL1" -> declaration + usage

# completion marks -------------------------------------------------------
6:1 completion   config-if scope (inside the interface body)

# documentSymbol marks ---------------------------------------------------
0:0 documentSymbol full outline (cursor is irrelevant; 0:0 is the placeholder)
